    "notes": {
        "d8e3d929-5333-4226-b639-7554369fe01d": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 160,
            "width": 384,
            "height": 224,
            "content": "## Test data assumption\n\nThe query-parameter lane filters Accounts with `where Code==\"400\"` and expects the first account to be **400 (Advertising)**, part of Xero's default chart of accounts. Unfiltered, Xero lists accounts by code, so 400 is never first (200 Sales is) \u2014 a dropped parameter fails the assertion. On an organisation without account 400, use another code that exists and is not the lowest.\n\nThe header lane sends `Accept: application/xml`; Xero then answers in XML, which proves the headers reach the API."
        }
